# Harness Gate — No Exceptions

Every change to this repo passes through the Meeseeks harness before it is committed.
This holds whether or not the session was brain-loaded.

## The Gate

After the suite is green and before the commit:

1. Run the harness against the change.
   - `./meeseeks/tools_core/scripts/meeseeks_loop.py` for an ordinary change
   - `./meeseeks/tools_core/scripts/meeseeks_spin.py` for anything structural
   (James runs it and reports the output. You write the invocation and read the result.)
2. Read `meeseeks/logs/sessions/<session_id>/findings.md`.
3. Every CONFIRMED finding is fixed, or declined in writing in that version's design doc
   with the reason it was declined.

## Hard Rules

- **The confidence percentage is not the gate.** The findings are. A 95% run with an
  unanswered CONFIRMED finding does not pass; a 60% run with a clean findings list does.
- A finding is never closed by rewording it. Close it with a code change or a written
  decline.
- If the harness cannot run (dead council seat, missing key), the gate is **not** waived —
  say so and stop. Check with `./meeseeks/tools_core/scripts/meeseeks_models.py`.
  A silent council member looks exactly like one who agreed.
- Skip the gate only when James says to skip it, in this session, in so many words.

## Why

The harness exists to catch what a single reader misses — it found the SMTP 4xx retry bug
in `src/delivery.py` that the full suite passed over. A review step that runs only when
someone remembers it is not a review step.

## Who runs the gate

The coding agent does not commit, merge, push, or open pull requests. It leaves
completed work uncommitted in the working tree and reports what it changed.

The harness gate is run by James, locally, before the work ships. An agent that
cannot reach ~/projects/meeseeks-venv and ~/.meeseeks/API_CONFIG.env must say so
and stop rather than treating the gate as waived — but it may still complete and
report the work, because it is not the thing that ships it.

## Findings are an artifact

meeseeks/logs/ is gitignored, so findings.md is not preserved. After any gate run,
copy the report to claude/findings-<version>.md and commit it with the change.
